    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d166-a1">

                <pb facs="0299" n="257" xml:id="pg257"/>

                <head>Lord Russell to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-04-22"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 22, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> In acknowledging the receipt of the further
                    letter which you did me the honor to address to me, on the 6th instant, on the
                    subject of the intercepted correspondence, I will merely add that, while
                    entirely assenting to the principles laid down in the authorities to which you
                    refer, I am still unable to perceive their application to any facts which have
                    occurred in this country within the cognizance of her Majesty’s government.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient,
                    humble servant.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>RUSSELL.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams</hi>, Esq.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
